==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Anubis the Unblemished''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Almighty Anubis''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Anubis the Protector is a backliner possessing mostly middling or unfavorable stats, with a very long attack animation, high speed which can cause him to speed clip, and a long recharge time being his biggest flaws, with most of his other stats being only marginally above or below the norm. While his DPS is good by Stories of Legend standards, he becomes outdone as a generic backliner by [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] once her True Form is unlocked.

To compensate for his shortcomings, Anubis has three abilities that attempt to give him some niches to work with; [[Zombie Killer]], [[Immune to Slow]] and [[Immune to Waves]]. Zombie Killer is obviously meant to make Anubis into a counter for [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], but when facing the burrowing dead his average knockback count becomes another point of weakness, and his slow attacks are even more likely to whiff. As a consequence, the only Zombies Anubis is sensible to use against are the ones that don't burrow or outrange him, i.e. [[Lord Gravey]] and [[Lophiiformes Angaburu]]. Immune to Slow is considerably more niche since very few enemies are totally reliant on inflicting the slow status effect, but Anubis is able to use it to good effect against [[Croakley]] and the aforementioned Lophiiformes Angaburu. Immune to Waves makes Anubis almost completely safe from [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave attack enemies]] and the [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]], since most have a much shorter range than him, as well as high endurance allowing Anubis to land attacks on them more reliably. Sadly, Anubis has the misfortune of sharing the anti-wave DPS niche with a Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]], whom with Attack Buff Lv.10 nearly ties Anubis' DPS despite costing roughly half as much and recharging in about a seventh of the time. While it does cost 200 NP to raise Dancer Cat to this point, any player who hasn't already made this investment should be planning to due to just how powerful and accessible Dancer Cat is. By comparison, Anubis only has 95 higher range and the ability to reposition twice before dying compared to Dancer Cat's zero, though Dancer has a much lower cooldown. In summary, while Anubis performs acceptably as long as his attack animation is worked around, he is far from spectacular at anything.

==='''True Form'''===
Almighty Anubis receives a 25% boost to his health and attack, as well as [[Immune to Knockback|Immunity to Knockback]]. His attack power improvement barely raises his DPS above that of Awakened Ururun, and the health boost does little. Immune to knockback is largely a nerf to Anubis' performance as the ability to reposition from the knockback is more valuable than niche cases where it could be useful (e.g. [[Mr. Mole]]), though this allows him to get hits on enemies much easier without being interrupted, but is otherwise worse for survivability. Due to the Epic Catfruit Seed that is required to unlock his True Form being locked behind Uncanny Legends, it does not make him a great, or even good generalist over other Ubers that can use an Epic Catfruit Seed.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Immune to Surge]]''' is Almighty Anubis' best Talent, making him one of the few backliners with Surge Immunity. This Talent is practically a requirement for slow-recharging cats when dealing with various Surge-based enemies in the lategame, and helps immensely with several boss enemies, including [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Master Uril]], [[Kappy Jr.]] and [[Kappy Kawano]]. Immediately following is gaining his very own '''[[Surge Attack]]''', which on average increases Anubis' DPS by 1.3x (1.56x in combination with Attack Buff), however it has the caveat of relying on RNG for the Surge to spawn, in addition to many [[:Category:Enemies with Surge Immunity|Surge Immune Enemies]]—which includes many [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemies and a few bosses. However, outside these enemies and bosses, it's rather inconsistent and only worthwhile if you have a surplus of NP to spare. The least useful Talent for Anubis is [[Barrier Breaker]] (70% chance), as there is no shortage of reliable Barrier Breakers, not to mention the [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast Cannon]] making this Talent rather redundant.

His '''Attack Buff''' and '''Defense Buff''' Talents are worthwhile improvements to his stats, but he should be supplemented with [[Catseye]]s first if you ever want to get more mileage out of him.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
'''Attack Frequency Up''' is Almighty Anubis' best Ultra Talent, raising his Attack Frequency to a blazing-fast 5.23 seconds and his DPS at Lv.60 from 12.6k to 21.4k, or roughly a ~70% increase in DPS. This Ultra Talent, along with Attack Buff and Surge Attack, sees his average DPS jump to an impressive 33.4k DPS if all three are unlocked. The second Ultra Talent, '''[[Shield Piercing]]''', when combined with Surge Immunity, Anubis gains a very powerful niche against Aku enemies while resisting their Death Surges. When paired with Attack Frequency Up, he'll Pierce Shields on average every 7.5 seconds, making him competent at demolishing Aku enemies. Combined with his high DPH, he can 2-3 shot most threatening Akus. '''Cost Down''' is the least worthwhile of Anubis' Ultra Talents, as there are much better uses of NP, which makes this Talent rather redundant.

However, Anubis still isn't without his flaws; his Shield Pierce isn't at 100% which can occasionally make him unreliable when it truly counts, and whilst not normally an issue, his long foreswing can make him struggle against very high-KB enemies, like [[Rain D.]] His gains may be huge, but they come at an exorbitant price tag that can potentially put off many players. These Ultra Talents may be flashy, and the numbers may be high, but consider all your options before sinking your NP and Dark Catseyes into this canine.

==='''Orb'''===
Due to Almighty Anubis being an offensive generalist, Attack Up talent orbs may be useful. If you choose to unlock his Shield Piercing Ultra Talent, you may consider Aku Attack orbs to get a little more damage in. Berserker Orb is his best ability orb as a nuker backline.

