==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Anubis the Unblemished was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Advent of the Almighty (Removed Combo)|Advent of the Almighty]] and [[Infernal Power (Removed Combo)|Infernal Power]].
*[[Version 5.1 Update|Version 5.1]] decreased Anubis' foreswing from 5 seconds to 3.87 seconds.
*Anubis received [[Immune to Slow]] in [[Version 5.3 Update|Version 5.3]].
*Anubis received [[Zombie Killer]] in [[Version 5.7 Update|Version 5.7]].
*Prior to [[Version 12.7 Update|Version 12.7]], Anubis' Attack Frequency Up Ultra Talent reduced his time between attacks by roughly 15.2f <sup>0.507s</sup> per level up to 152f <sup>5.07s</sup>, not only considerably longer than the amount of idle time which can be reduced from his attack cycle (110f <sup>3.67s</sup>) but longer than his backswing and idle durations combined by one frame. This meant that upgrades past level 8 had no practical impact on his performance outside of highly unlikely scenarios. He along with [[Coppermine (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Coppermine κ]] were the only units affected by this excessive progression before this version.
*[[wikipedia:Anubis|Anubis]] is the Egyptian God of funerary rites who also protects graves. He was also the one responsible for taking souls to the afterlife.
**The actual Egyptin God of Death is [[wikipedia:Osiris|Osiris]].
**Anubis's relation to the dead is likely the reason for his Zombie Killer ability in-game.
*Anubis the Protector was the first unit with the [[Immune to Waves]] ability.
*Anubis the Protector is one of the units to have his descriptions rewritten in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], as "Unharmed by wave attacks" was changed to "Immune to Waves".

